            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            monad restricts to the full subcategory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
            where we can construct a factorization of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            monad which allows us to understand how
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            algebras arise via expectation maps.
          %p
            Let us first note a relationship between the Giry monad on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+monad"} Radon monad
